Great question — this is a core part of designing your JPA entity relationships correctly.

---

## ✅ Situation:

You have a structure like this:

> **One Course → Many Class\_Course**
> (i.e., one course is taught in multiple classes/sections)

---

## ✅ Where to Place `@OneToMany`

You put the `@OneToMany` **on the “one” side**, i.e., on the `Course` entity, because **a single course maps to many `Class_Course` entities**.

### 🔧 `Course.java` – owns the OneToMany

```java
@OneToMany(mappedBy = "course_class", cascade = CascadeType.ALL)
private List<Class_Course> course_class = new ArrayList<>();
```

Explanation:

* `mappedBy = "course_class"` points to the field in `Class_Course` that maps back to `Course`.
* You don’t need a `@JoinColumn` here because this is the inverse side of the `@ManyToOne`.

---

### 🔧 `Class_Course.java` – owns the ManyToOne

```java
@ManyToOne
@JoinColumn(name = "course_id") // This will create a foreign key in class_course table
private Course course_class;
```

Explanation:

* This side **owns the relationship** and is responsible for the join column (`course_id` foreign key).

---

## 🧠 Think of it Like This:

| Entity         | Relationship                         | Annotation                                   |
| -------------- | ------------------------------------ | -------------------------------------------- |
| `Course`       | One course has many class sessions   | `@OneToMany(mappedBy = "course_class")`      |
| `Class_Course` | Each class session is for one course | `@ManyToOne @JoinColumn(name = "course_id")` |

---

## ✅ Example

```java
// Course.java
@Entity
public class Course {
    @Id
    @GeneratedValue(strategy = GenerationType.IDENTITY)
    private Long id;

    private String courseName;

    @OneToMany(mappedBy = "course_class", cascade = CascadeType.ALL)
    private List<Class_Course> course_class = new ArrayList<>();
}
```

```java
// Class_Course.java
@Entity
public class Class_Course {
    @Id
    @GeneratedValue(strategy = GenerationType.IDENTITY)
    private Long id;

    @ManyToOne
    @JoinColumn(name = "course_id")
    private Course course_class;

    // other fields
}
```

---

## ✅ Bonus: Data Insertion Example

```java
Course course = new Course();
course.setCourseName("Operating Systems");

Class_Course cc1 = new Class_Course();
cc1.setTime(Time.valueOf("09:00:00"));
cc1.setSemester(1L);
cc1.setCourse_class(course); // connect class to course

Class_Course cc2 = new Class_Course();
cc2.setTime(Time.valueOf("11:00:00"));
cc2.setSemester(1L);
cc2.setCourse_class(course);

course.setCourse_class(Arrays.asList(cc1, cc2)); // link course to its classes

courseRepo.save(course); // saves everything due to cascade
```

